arm64: dts: rockchip: khadas-edge: HDMI on the big VOP

Khadas Edge1, Android 14 on mainline 6.12. Applied to kernel/mainline by
build/build-kernel.sh before every build (device/khadas/edge/kernel/patches/).

The RK3399's HDMI encoder can take either display controller. Mainline's
display-subsystem lists the little VOP first, so it is CRTC 0, and both the
kernel's fbdev and drm_hwcomposer give HDMI the first CRTC it supports. The
little VOP has one window besides the cursor: drm_hwcomposer had a single
plane, and card 27's SurfaceFlinger dump shows every layer of every frame
composed by the GPU ("Comp Type CLIENT" for all four layers while a video
played; composition efficiency 0.07 since boot) - video, app, dialog and
overlay redrawn into a 1080p buffer 60 times a second.

The big VOP has three planes (win0 and win1 with NV12 and scaling, win2 RGB)
and outputs up to 4096x2160. Rockchip's DT for the Edge disables HDMI's
little-VOP endpoint (hdmi_in_vopl) for this; mainline's graph walk
(of_graph_get_next_endpoint, drm_of_find_possible_crtcs) ignores an
endpoint's status, so the little VOP itself is disabled - rockchip-drm skips
an unavailable VOP in "ports". Nothing else on this board uses it: no DSI,
eDP or DP output is enabled in its DT. boot.scr turns it back on with
"vop=lit" in edge1-options.txt.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-khadas-edge.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-khadas-edge.dtsi
index 97d8accd5..8ea31a0dd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-khadas-edge.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-khadas-edge.dtsi
@@ -924,3 +924,23 @@ &vdec {
 	assigned-clocks = <&cru SCLK_VDU_CA>, <&cru SCLK_VDU_CORE>;
 	assigned-clock-rates = <400000000>, <400000000>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * HDMI from the big VOP. The RK3399 has two display controllers and the HDMI
+ * encoder can take either; display-subsystem lists the little one first, so it
+ * is CRTC 0 and drives HDMI. It has one window apart from the cursor: the
+ * Android compositor (drm_hwcomposer) gets a single plane and composes every
+ * layer of every frame on the GPU, video included. The big VOP has three - two
+ * with NV12 and scaling - and goes to 4096x2160. Rockchip's own DT for the Edge
+ * disables HDMI's little-VOP endpoint for the same reason; mainline's graph code
+ * does not honour an endpoint's status, so the little VOP goes. Nothing else on
+ * this board uses it (no DSI, eDP or DP is enabled). "vop=lit" in
+ * edge1-options.txt turns it back on (boot.scr).
+ */
+&vopl {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&vopl_mmu {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
